{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Alacer performance contracts (M5, architecture §18 / ADR-0011). Every criterion benchmark in the workspace is published as a baseline in benchmarks/baselines/baselines.json and gated here. `budgets` are architecture gates expressed as ratios of criterion medians — host-independent, enforced everywhere. `regressions` are per-case median gates against the published baseline, scoped `same-host`: absolute times only compare on the recorded host fingerprint (os/arch/cpu model/count); foreign hosts — CI runners — skip them and rely on criterion's own previous-run comparison plus the ratio budgets. Adding a benchmark case without publishing its baseline and regression gate fails the M5 exit suite.",
  "tolerance_default": 0.25,
  "budgets": [
    {
      "id": "w1_incremental_speedup",
      "metric": "median_ratio",
      "numerator": "w1/full_rebuild",
      "denominator": "w1/incremental_churn_10pct",
      "op": ">=",
      "budget": 2.0,
      "cite": "architecture §18 M2 exit gate (W1 ≥ 2× vs full relayout), ADR-0008; test-enforced in alacer-layout/tests/w1_gate.rs, here measured by criterion"
    },
    {
      "id": "input_storm_batching",
      "metric": "median_ratio",
      "numerator": "input/storm_50_moves_direct",
      "denominator": "input/storm_50_moves_queued",
      "op": ">=",
      "budget": 2.0,
      "cite": "architecture §10.2 (input storms cost one frame of work, not N events), ADR-0014; the queued batch routes one coalesced event where the pre-M8 wiring dispatched all 50"
    },
    {
      "id": "a11y_incremental_speedup",
      "metric": "median_ratio",
      "numerator": "a11y/full_rebuild_1k",
      "denominator": "a11y/incremental_1k_dirty_10pct",
      "op": ">=",
      "budget": 2.0,
      "cite": "architecture §11.1 item 4 (never a full-tree rebuild per frame — the egui cost we refuse), ADR-0015; the M9 shape drains the sink's dirty-only delta where the pre-M9 window rebuilt the whole tree per a11y frame"
    }
  ],
